WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:10.962
Hi! Don't panic when you meet a new word! The sentence often hides clues. Today we'll learn vocabulary in context.

2
00:00:11.112 --> 00:00:15.186
First read the whole sentence, before and after the ___.

3
00:00:15.336 --> 00:00:19.218
After and or also, the idea is often similar.

4
00:00:19.368 --> 00:00:23.058
After but, the idea is often the opposite.

5
00:00:23.208 --> 00:00:28.554
Because and so tell you why, and that helps you guess the word.

6
00:00:28.704 --> 00:00:33.114
First guess in your own words: should it be happy or sad here?

7
00:00:33.264 --> 00:00:39.042
Check what kind of word fits: after a we need a noun, after very we need an adjective.

8
00:00:39.192 --> 00:00:42.666
Put each option into the sentence and read it.

9
00:00:42.816 --> 00:00:46.938
Choose the one that makes the most sense.

10
00:00:47.088 --> 00:00:52.770
Watch out! Looking at one word and not the whole sentence leads to mistakes!

11
00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:59.130
The soup is hot, that's the cause, so she drinks it slowly. Slowly is correct.

12
00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:04.362
After choosing, always read the whole sentence again.

13
00:01:04.512 --> 00:01:14.586
Your turn! Sam was, ___, because he lost his toy. Which one? Pause and think.

14
00:01:14.736 --> 00:01:20.754
Losing a toy makes you sad, so upset. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:20.904 --> 00:01:31.242
Another one! The room was dark, so Dad switched on the, ___. Which one? Pause and think.

16
00:01:31.392 --> 00:01:37.554
The room is dark, so he switches on the light. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:37.704 --> 00:01:48.450
Here's another! The test was easy, but the last question was, ___. Which one? Pause and think.

18
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:55.554
But shows the opposite, and the opposite of easy is difficult. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:55.704 --> 00:02:06.762
Try one more! Please, ___, the plants every morning so they do not dry up. Which one? Pause and think.

20
00:02:06.912 --> 00:02:12.498
So they don't dry up, we water them. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:12.648 --> 00:02:23.898
Try one more! The puppy is very, ___. It runs and jumps all day. Which one? Pause and think.

22
00:02:24.048 --> 00:02:30.018
Running and jumping all day means it's active. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:30.168 --> 00:02:40.290
Try one more! It was so, ___, that we turned on the fan. Which one? Pause and think.

24
00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:45.906
We turn on the fan when it is hot. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:46.056 --> 00:02:56.394
Last one! Grandpa needs his, ___, to read small words. Which one? Pause and think.

26
00:02:56.544 --> 00:03:02.466
To read small words he needs glasses. Did you get it right?

27
00:03:02.616 --> 00:03:12.354
Remember: read the whole sentence, find clues like and, but, because and so, guess the meaning, check the word type, then try each option.

28
00:03:12.504 --> 00:03:18.161
Next time you meet a new word in a story, use the clues to guess!

